Two signals, both deliberately clock-free:
\itemize{
\item A name tagged \verb{@export} in a roxygen block that does not appear in
\code{NAMESPACE}. This is the real cost of a forgotten \code{document()} call: the
function is not exported, so users cannot call it, and \verb{R CMD check} says
nothing because a package is free to export whatever it likes.
\item An \code{.Rd} file whose roxygen2 backlink names a source file that no longer
exists, which is the orphan left behind when a source file is renamed or
deleted without re-documenting.
